 "text": "Hello there! How's your day treating you? Something from the 50s or 60s usually gives you the basics without going too far. Do you want classic like Rock and Roll at School, or something with a beat like At the Ball? Then go for something swinging like In My Rough Way or So Far So Good. Jazz is great for showing off your own style without being too prescriptive. Oh, I did a double take. Which one did you like, the swinging one or the easy one? Then ask at the club if you can go for a dance. Roughly ten pounds for few hours dancing, which includes the band. It' worth it for the experience. Nice and cheap, just make sure it' a good one and everyone knows the steps.",
